WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:00.540
RENE GARCIA
FRANCESCHINI: My name

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:02.310
is Rene Garcia Franceschini.

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.890
I'm a junior in the Department
of Civil and Environmental

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:05.820
Engineering.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.710
And my work concerns
routing of drones

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:10.020
in communications-constrained
environments.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.410
So drones are being used
currently more and more

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.270
to inspect
infrastructure, especially

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:17.100
after emergency situations.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.990
Well, there's two
problems with using drones

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.080
to inspect infrastructure.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.300
One of them is that a lot
of critical infrastructure,

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.660
such as pipelines that's
in rural areas, where

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.690
4G LTE or GPS coverage
might be spottier.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.750
And the second problem is
that in emergency situations,

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.650
a lot of cell towers are
down, such that 4G LTE

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.240
signal is unreliable.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.740
So the problem we're
trying to solve

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:40.320
is, how do we
better route drones

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.170
to inspect infrastructure in
these communications-uncertain

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.220
environments?

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:50.130
And our approach combines work
in team orienteering algorithms

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.080
with creating
learning methods such

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.570
that the drones
are simultaneously

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.430
inspecting nodes,
while also learning

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.460
about the communications
space of the map

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.590
to learn what the
communications coverage is

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:02.820
at different points.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:06.330
And our results show that
there is both an increase

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.490
in the total score at
the end of the simulation

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:12.760
and also a decrease in
computational time towards--

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:14.940
at the end of the simulation.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.590
And this work
could ultimately be

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:20.780
used to make infrastructure
monitoring quicker and safer.

